    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d628">

                <pb facs="0991" n="871" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg871"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">574.G1/873: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation (Sykes) to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-10-04T17:00:00+00:00">October 4, 1932—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 4—2:28 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. (1) Delegation confidentially informed that Soviet delegates are planning to
                    invite next combined conference to meet in Russia. Please instruct whether
                    delegation should endeavor to prevent such invitation from being extended or
                    accepted and what position it should take if invitation is extended.</p>
                <p>(2) At the time of signature of convention should delegation make statement
                    relative to unrecognized regimes similar to that made at London Safety of Life
                    at Sea Conference?<anchor n="17" xml:id="d628-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sykes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d628-f1" n="17" xml:id="d628-f1-content">
                <p>See instruction of March 28, 1929, to the American delegation, <ref
